The data routine
READ (1 min): read the STEM fully — underline the IV, DV and units; study EVERY table row and axis before touching questions. PLAN (30 s): note which module each sub-question raids; jot the 2–3 points each mark needs. ANSWER: calculations show FORMULA → SUBSTITUTION → ANSWER + UNITS (method marks survive arithmetic slips); % change = (change ÷ original) × 100; means exclude ANOMALIES (circle and note them — never silently delete); rates = quantity ÷ time. GRAPHS: axes (IV-X, DV-Y, units), 3/4-page scales, small precise plots, best-fit line/curve, title. CHECK (last 5 min of paper): units, contradictions, unanswered parts, candidate details. PAPER STRATEGY: first pass — all confident questions; second pass — hard ones with fresh eyes; never leave blanks; if stuck >3 min, mark and move.$wdthseed$, NULL, 30, 4, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Apply the READ-PLAN-ANSWER routine to data questions","Calculate percentages, means and rates correctly","Execute a full-paper timing plan"],"introduction":"Data questions panic students who memorised notes but never practised thinking. A routine replaces panic — read, plan, answer, check.","key_points":["Four-step routine","Calculation presentation","Two-pass paper strategy"],"references":["WOLI DAN TECH HUB original — data-question workbook (see practical)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod11$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod11:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, m