Twenty definitions
Cover the right column; recall; check. (1) Diffusion — net movement of particles from high to low concentration down a gradient. (2) Osmosis — net movement of water from high to low water concentration across a partially permeable membrane. (3) Active transport — movement against a gradient using ATP and carriers. (4) Enzyme — specific protein catalyst with an active site, unchanged by reaction. (5) Denaturation — irreversible loss of 3D shape (heat/extreme pH) destroying function. (6) Photosynthesis — CO2 + water → glucose + oxygen using light and chlorophyll. (7) Aerobic respiration — glucose + oxygen → CO2 + water + large energy. (8) Gene — DNA section coding one trait. (9) Allele — one version of a gene. (10) Genotype — allele pair carried; phenotype — trait expressed. (11) Mitosis — one division → 2 identical diploid cells (growth/repair). (12) Meiosis — two divisions → 4 unique haploid cells (gametes). (13) Natural selection — variation + competition + differential survival + inheritance shifting allele frequencies. (14) Species — interbreeding group producing fertile offspring. (15) Ecosystem — community plus non-living environment. (16) Trophic level — feeding step from producers. (17) Homeostasis — maintaining constant internal conditions by negative feedback. (18) Reflex — fast involuntary response via receptor→sensory→relay→motor→effector. (19) Transpiration — water loss from leaves driving xylem pull. (20) Germination — sprouting requiring water + oxygen + warmth.

Four equations, zero confusion
PHOTOSYNTHESIS: 6CO2 + 6H2O →(light/chlorophyll) C6H12O6 + 6O2. AEROBIC RESPIRATION: C6H12O6 + 6O2 → 6CO2 + 6H2O + energy (~30 ATP). ANAEROBIC (muscle): glucose → lactic acid + small energy. ANAEROBIC (yeast): glucose → ethanol + CO2 + small energy. Direction discipline: photosynthesis BUILDS glucose (needs input); respiration BREAKS it (releases output). Common swap: writing respiration's arrow for photosynthesis — check every equation's direction before moving on. Word equations earn full marks where symbols are not demanded; add symbols only when confident.$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 1, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Write all 20 definitions word-perfect from memory","Write all 4 equations with correct direction","Self-test with cover-and-recall cycles"],"introduction":"Examiners cannot mark what they cannot recognise. These definitions and equations are the currency of every biology paper — mint them now.","key_points":["Recall blind, mark harshly","Name the membrane/ATP/site","Space the drills"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — glossary (verify every definition)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod12$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod12:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
