The six diagrams
(1) PLANT CELL: wall, membrane, cytoplasm, nucleus, vacuole, chloroplast, mitochondrion — rectangular with even walls. (2) ANIMAL CELL: membrane, cytoplasm, nucleus, mitochondrion — rounded, NO wall/vacuole/chloroplasts. (3) HEART (double circulation): four chambers, aorta/vena cava/pulmonary vessels, valves, arrows showing flow + O2 colours. (4) LEAF SECTION: cuticle, upper epidermis, palisade, spongy + air spaces, lower epidermis with stomata/guard cells, vein (xylem above, phloem below). (5) FLOWER (half-section): sepals, petals, anther/filament, stigma/style/ovary/ovule. (6) REFLEX ARC: receptor → sensory → spinal cord relay → motor → muscle, with CNS box and direction arrows. RULES (Module 10): large, sharp pencil, single lines, no shading, ruled touching labels, title + magnification. Annotate ONE function per label where space allows ('xylem — carries water up').$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 2, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Draw and label six key diagrams from memory","Apply biological drawing rules automatically","Annotate diagrams with functions, not just names"],"introduction":"A perfect diagram can earn 6 marks in 3 minutes — the best rate in the paper. These six appear year after year.","key_points":["Six diagrams cold","Timed redraws","Function annotations"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — figures in Chapters 4, 30, 32, 34, 39"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod12$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod12:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.i